# The publish-audit deny list. NOT committed, deliberately: it spells out the
# exact strings it exists to keep out of the repository, and the single
# character classes that stop it matching itself during a scan do nothing to
# stop a person reading it. Continuous integration gets these rules from a
# repository secret instead. See .publish-audit.example.json for the schema.
.publish-audit.json

.superpowers/

# Agent guidance and the design archive: kept on disk, out of the repo.
# The published tree is the plugin, its tests, its tooling and its README.
CLAUDE.md
docs/CLAUDE-HISTORY.md
# Draft text for posting elsewhere (Discord, upstream issues). Internal
# working documents, not part of the published plugin. The CLAUDE-PROMPT-
# prefix keeps them inside the workspace notes backup sweep, which matches
# docs/CLAUDE-*.md; a name outside that pattern would have no backup and no
# git coverage at all.
docs/CLAUDE-PROMPT-*.md
docs/superpowers/
